.TH MD_GET_CHARACTERS 3 "2026-10-16" "libmorsedec 0.2.0" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
md_get_characters \- borrow a channel message snapshot with character metadata
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <morsedec.h>

int md_get_characters(const morsedec_decoder_t *decoder, uint64_t
    id, const struct morsedec_character **characters, size_t
    *count);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Borrow a channel message snapshot with character metadata.
.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I decoder
Decoder handle. Calls using this handle must be serialized, including queries.
.TP
.I id
Stable channel ID, or zero to request the current channel.
.TP
.I characters
Non-NULL output address for a read-only borrowed array. Do not free or modify
the array.
.TP
.I count
Non-NULL output address for the number of records; there is no terminator
record.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns MORSEDEC_SUCCESS (1) on success, or MORSEDEC_FAILURE (0) and sets
errno on failure. Do not inspect errno after success.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
NULL decoder, characters or count.
.TP
.B ENOENT
Nonzero id does not identify a currently tracked channel.
.SH REMARKS
Returns the current bounded message snapshot, at most
MORSEDEC_MESSAGE_CAPACITY (500) records. If id is zero and there is no current
channel, returns success with *characters=NULL and *count=0. A named live
channel may also have zero characters.
.PP
The view is valid only until the next mutating call on this handle, including
processing, reset, flush, pin/unpin or deletion. Copy records while access to
the handle is serialized if they are needed later. Channel retirement
invalidates that channel ID.
.PP
Records contain Latin-1 character bytes, word-type labels, source ordinals,
low-SNR flags and revisable word-boundary metadata. These are snapshots, not a
queue of newly arrived characters. Preserve an archive keyed by channel ID and
ordinal, applying revisions rather than blindly appending repeated snapshots.
Consume frequently: oldest records are discarded as the bounded buffer fills,
and retired channel messages are no longer available. See libmorsedec(3) for
all record fields.
.SH THREAD SAFETY
Serialize all calls that access the same handle, including getters. Different
handles may process concurrently after construction. These functions are not
specified as async-signal-safe.
.SH VERSION
This md_ entry point is available since libmorsedec 0.2.0 (shared-library ABI
1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmorsedec (3),
.BR md_get_text (3),
.BR md_get_channel (3),
.BR md_flush (3),
.BR md_reset (3)
